Chapter: InlineCostBased

 The opt-in cost-based inliner (`passes=+inline-cost-based`, via the
 `.flags` sidecar) over the exact shape that found its template-reuse
 defect. `make-pbox` is a record-building candidate with two call
 sites; `subst-once`'s record arm used to `__record-set` the
 candidate's body template in place, so the first site's argument
 replaced the field value for every later site, splicing the first
 caller's locals into a function that does not bind them (CDX2040
 `Unresolved call` at emit, or silently the wrong record). The
 assertion that matters is the SECOND caller's record carrying the
 SECOND caller's values. `pick2` rides along as the branchy
 arithmetic shape the leaf pass refuses (it has an `if`) and the
 cost pass takes.

Section: Candidates

  PBox = record {
   first : Integer,
   second : Integer,
   tag : Integer
  }

  make-pbox : Integer, Integer -> PBox
  make-pbox (a) (b) = PBox { first = a, second = b, tag = 7 }

  pick2 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pick2 (a) (b) = if a > b then a else b

Section: Callers

  caller-one : Integer
  caller-one =
   let x = 11
   in let y = 22
   in let bx = make-pbox x y
   in bx.first * 100 + bx.second

  caller-two : Integer
  caller-two =
   let p = 33
   in let q = 44
   in let bx = make-pbox p q
   in bx.first * 100 + bx.second + bx.tag

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   let a = caller-one
   in let b = caller-two
   in let c = pick2 5 9
   in let d = pick2 40 2
   in print-line-uni ("inline-cost-based: " & show a & " " & show b & " " & show c & " " & show d)
  end
